    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2CYyGtgLvq5iRgHjYX2SJe6)_\n\n## Summary\n\n- Candidate width now follows the posframe (`sp-posframe-width-fraction` of the frame) instead of the whole frame; `sp-citations-candidate-margin` keeps 2 columns free.\n- All template columns are `*` columns. Each column is fitted to the longest value among all entries (so rows stay aligned): narrow columns (citekey, year, type) keep their full width, and the title, authors and tags share the rest.\n- New year column after the authors; a column empty for every entry (e.g. `beref`) is dropped with its spacing.\n- Cut text stays hidden in the candidate, so matching still sees the full title and authors.\n- Implemented as `:around` advice on `citar--format-candidates` (`sp-citations--format-candidates`); templates without a `*` column fall back to citar's own function.\n- Docs updated in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-academic.org` (bullet lists); `sp-citations.el` is the matching tangle. No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Only the width and assembly helpers were run, in batch Emacs with stubs (sizes add up, empty column dropped). The advice itself was not run against real citar; please try `citar-open` with the posframe on.\n- Branch name has no PR number prefix (cannot rename from the cloud session).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9m8fmtgNiBeMPZDGW)_",
